Wait — there's a bug in my test: I wrote

```cpp
draft.clear();
QVERIFY2(m_db->commitDraft(draft->id, fields, nullptr, &error), qPrintable(error));
Q_UNUSED(draft);
const int committedId = draft->id;
```

`draft.clear()` on an optional sets it to nullopt; then draft->id after clear is UB/problematic (accessing nullopt → assert in debug). And calling commitDraft(draft->id, ...) after clear() is wrong. Fix: capture id first.

```cpp
const int draftId = draft->id;
draft.reset();
QVERIFY2(m_db->commitDraft(draftId, fields, nullptr, &error), ...);
const int committedId = draftId;
```

Let me fix that now. `std::optional::clear()` exists (aliases reset). But accessing draft->id after reset is UB. Fix it.

